# 4-Bit Counter: RTL-to-GDSII ASIC Implementation

## Overview

This project demonstrates the complete implementation of a 4-bit synchronous counter through an RTL-to-GDSII ASIC design flow using open-source EDA tools and the Sky130 Process Design Kit (PDK).

The design was developed in Verilog, functionally verified through simulation, synthesized using Yosys, physically implemented using OpenLane 2/OpenROAD, and verified through DRC and LVS before generating the final GDSII layout.

---

## Design Specification

### Inputs

* `clk` : Clock input
* `rst` : Active-high reset

### Outputs

* `count[3:0]` : 4-bit counter output

### Functionality

* Counter increments on every positive clock edge.
* Counter resets to `0000` when reset is asserted.

